  "comment": "**What it does**\nThe O'Shaughnessy small-cap value-and-momentum combo: cheap on sales AND already winning.\n- **Your choices:** $300M-$2B, cheap on sales versus peers, RS Rank 70+, revenue growing, tradeable volume, volatility expected.\n- Sales-based on purpose \u2014 small companies often aren't profitable yet, and that is fine here.\n- **Note:** P/S has no peer-comparison column in the database, so 'cheaper than its industry' is expressed as the peer-ranked P/S Score (70+ = cheaper than ~70% of its peer group). Same idea, correctly wired.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- Widen it: drop the P/S Score from 70 to 50 (merely mid-priced rather than cheap).\n- Tighten it: raise `rs_rank` from 70 to 85 for only the strongest movers.\n- Go smaller: lower the `market_cap` band to $100M-$1B \u2014 expect thinner liquidity.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- Sort by `momentum_score`, tiebreak `growth_score`.\n- Avoid sorting by `value_score` (the P/S test already handles cheapness) and `quality_score` (small caps often aren't profitable yet \u2014 that's accepted here).\n\n_Built 2026-08-13 \u00b7 134 matches at build time._",
  "ai_instructions": "Find small companies that are cheap on sales AND already winning \u2014 the\nO'Shaughnessy small-cap growth & value combo (the best long-run track record of\nthe classic screens).\n- **Goal**: growth + value combo. **Dividends**: ignore.\n- **Size**: small caps, roughly $300M-$2B.\n- **Cheap on sales**: price-to-sales below its industry (sales-based on purpose \u2014\n  small companies often aren't profitable yet, and that is FINE here).\n- **Already winning**: strong recent price strength (RS Rank 70+), revenue growing.\n- **Tradeable**: enough daily volume to get in and out.\n- **Risk**: volatile is expected. **Kinds**: normal stocks only.\n- **Results**: ~50-200 names. **Sorting**: momentum first, tiebreak growth.",
